// What the cosigner needs from the runtime it runs inside.
//
// Its own world, rather than an edited copy of `enclave:tasks`'s: the WIT under `deps/` is copied
// byte for byte from the runtime's `wit/`, and the wallet's e2e, on a real runtime, is what shows
// the two still fit. A guest that wants two capabilities composes them here instead of editing
// either.
//
// Not yet generated from. The crate now builds as a wasm32-wasip2 component — `nix build .#policy`
// — serving gRPC over `wasi:http/incoming-handler`, which removed the reason this could not be
// generated. What remains is composing this world with the one `wstd::http_server` exports, so
// `src/host.rs` still mirrors these signatures behind a trait and `tests/wit_test.rs` checks the
// mirror against this file. Wiring `wit_bindgen::generate!` over this world replaces the trait's
// `Detached` impl and is the last step.
package vtxos:cosigner@0.1.0;

world cosigner {
    // `run-task`, plus the queue to arm it with. The cosigner uses this for one thing: a settle
    // that has come due. Where the image allowlists the ASP the task executes the sealed delegate
    // itself; where it does not, it reads the delegate, compares the deadline to the clock, and
    // wakes its owner instead. Egress is the image's to grant, and is not named in this world.
    include enclave:tasks/background@0.1.0;

    // Waking those devices. The cosigner never sees a token and never sends a message; it spends
    // an enrolment an interactive call already made.
    import enclave:notify/notify@0.1.0;

    // The wallet key, held by the runtime: the cosigner asks for its FROST rounds and holds no
    // share of its own.
    import enclave:signer/wallet@0.1.0;

    // Spans to X-Ray and metrics to CloudWatch, attributed by the runtime to the tenant this
    // invocation runs for.
    //
    // Free until it is called. An interface the code never calls is not an import of the built
    // component — checked with `wasm-tools component wit` on the release build, whose imports were
    // identical with and without this line — so the cosigner still instantiates on a runtime
    // without telemetry, and only starts to need one from its first call.
    include enclave:telemetry/observed@0.1.0;
}
